title: edit --status bypasses require_claim and every other move rule
updated: 2026-08-10T01:27:58Z
---

`Cmd/Edit.pm:156` writes the status directly; `Cmd/Move.pm:103` enforces
`require_claim` first. Two code paths for "change the status", and they
contradict each other:

    karr move 1 in-progress          -> "Status 'in-progress' requires --claim"  rc=1
    karr edit 1 --status in-progress -> "Updated task 1"                          rc=0
    karr edit 1 --status ZZZ         -> "Updated task 1"                          rc=0

The `require_claim` guarantee that the whole multi-agent coordination rests on
is bypassable in one line, by accident as easily as on purpose.

Fix: funnel both through one status-change path that applies the same rules
(validation, require_claim, lifecycle timestamps, WIP once that exists). This is
the drift-between-duplicated-concepts pattern; the fix should remove the
duplicate rather than copy the checks into `edit`.
Fixed and merged into main; full suite green at 88 files / 566 tests.

Every one of these was reproduced before it was fixed and left a regression test
that was verified to fail against the pre-fix code -- not a test that merely
passes now. Details and what was deliberately NOT fixed are in the merge commit
that names this ticket.
